# Headless Game CI/CD & Build Automation

This skill provides automated headless build scripts, asset cooking pipelines, and test runners for continuous integration (GitHub Actions, local CLI daemons) across major video game engines.

---

## 1. Godot 4 Headless CI Automation

Export game binaries and execute unit tests headlessly without an X11/Wayland display server:

```bash
# 1. Import and bake assets headlessly
godot --headless --editor --quit

# 2. Run GUT (Godot Unit Testing) suite
godot --headless -s addons/gut/gut_cmdln.gd -gdir=res://tests/ -gexit

# 3. Export dedicated release build for Linux and Windows
godot --headless --export-release "Linux/X11" build/linux/mygame.x86_64
godot --headless --export-release "Windows Desktop" build/windows/mygame.exe
```

---

## 2. Unity Headless Batchmode Builds

Run Unity Editor in headless batchmode with automated log capture:

```bash
unity-editor \
  -batchmode \
  -nographics \
  -projectPath . \
  -executeMethod BuildPipelineScript.BuildStandaloneWindows64 \
  -quit \
  -logFile /tmp/unity_build.log

# Check exit code
if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then
  cat /tmp/unity_build.log | grep -E "error CS|Fatal Error"
  exit 1
fi
```

---

## 3. Unreal Engine 5 Headless Cook & Package

Automate UE5 builds using `RunUAT.sh` (Unreal Automation Tool):

```bash
"$UE5_DIR/Engine/Build/BatchFiles/RunUAT.sh" BuildCookRun \
  -project="$(pwd)/MyGame.uproject" \
  -platform=Linux \
  -clientconfig=Shipping \
  -cook \
  -build \
  -stage \
  -package \
  -archive \
  -archivedirectory="$(pwd)/dist" \
  -nocompileeditor \
  -nop4
```

